{
  "_comment": [
    "Synthetic by rule. Shapes follow",
    "https://docs.kraken.com/api/docs/rest-api/get-status-recent-withdrawals and",
    "https://docs.kraken.com/api/docs/rest-api/get-status-recent-deposits .",
    "",
    "These endpoints are the ONLY place the destination address and the network txid appear -- the",
    "Ledgers feed carries neither. `refid` is the join key back to the ledger row, `info` is the",
    "destination address and `txid` is the on-chain id. The withdrawal refid below is the same one",
    "kraken-ledgers-api.json's withdrawal row carries.",
    "",
    "The deposit block is deliberately the WRAPPED shape ({deposit: [...], next_cursor}) while the",
    "withdrawal block is a bare array: Kraken documents a cursor parameter but does not publish",
    "which shape it returns for withdrawals, so the reader accepts both and this fixture exercises",
    "both in one test.",
    "",
    "The ETH address is checksummed here on purpose. exchange_records stores addresses lowercased",
    "so an exchange withdrawal can join to the on-chain deposit it produced."
  ],
